WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.051 --> 00:00:02.009
ABHISHEK KASHYAP: We just
launched BigQuery ML,

00:00:02.009 --> 00:00:07.260
a new technology for machine
learning in BigQuery using SQL.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.750
Now you may ask, so what?

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.930
To illustrate, let us
take a marketing analyst

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.740
at a retail company.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:18.140
One of your projects,
a very typical project,

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.900
is to plan marketing
campaigns for website visitors

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.600
to drive them to come
back and purchase.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.170
There are 1 million
website visitors a month,

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:32.400
of which less than 1%
come back and purchase.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.410
You already know
that it's going to be

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.560
highly inefficient to
market to everyone.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.360
What you need is a way to rank
the visitors and then market

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.080
only to the top ones.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.880
How do you do that?

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.650
You need to build a
machine learning model

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.200
to rank these visitors.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.780
You have the website data
from Google Analytics.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.680
You have your sales database,
all in BigQuery already.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.080
But how do you build this model?

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.840
You'll likely need a
data scientist and a way

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.780
to move this data out
of your data warehouse.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.960
However, as is always
the case, your company

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.170
has a data science
team of 10, and they

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.390
are busy with other projects.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:15.270
That is where
BigQuery ML comes in.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:19.680
BigQuery ML enables
you to create a model

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.370
without having to move data,
or learning a new language,

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:26.430
or relying on capacity
from another team.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.450
Let's see this in action.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:32.280
You start by writing a
SQL query to select data

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.670
from the Google Analytics
table, which is illustrated here

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:39.810
through a public data set we
have for anyone to access.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.190
And you are going to love this.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:43.890
To do machine learning
on top, all you need

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:45.900
is two lines of SQL code--

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.700
CREATE MODEL and PREDICT.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:48.690
That's it.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:51.490
We'll CREATE MODEL,
give it a name.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:54.030
Tell us it is a logistic
regression model,

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:57.110
and it's going to predict
if a visitor will buy later.

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.310
With that, click Run query.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:03.630
The model is built, all
within BigQuery using SQL.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:07.860
Once the model is ready, just
write another simple SQL query

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:11.850
that will predict, using the
model name that you have given,

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:14.070
and get the predictions
on new visitors.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:17.430
From there, you can
build your BI reports

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:20.640
and take all marketing actions
you need to take on this code

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.080
visitor list.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.580
Cool, right?

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.670
Now let's see how
this model did.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:30.450
You will find that
re-marketing to just the top 6%

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:35.760
of the visitors provides a 9x
marketing ROI versus targeting

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.440
all visitors.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.370
And what more?

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:42.270
You still reach 50% of
the potential buyers

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.810
after targeting just
6% of the visitors.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:48.870
Now, that is an impressive
return with such little work.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:52.530
And you can further optimize
this by planning campaigns

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:56.490
where you spend more on higher
scored leads and less on lower.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:59.280
You may have noticed that
to get these results,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.180
no help was needed from
a data science team,

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.830
and you did not have
to move data, either,

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.780
to build this machine
learning model.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:10.680
All you did was to write
two lines of familiar SQL,

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.690
which you are an
expert at, and we

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:15.390
took care of everything
machine learning

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:17.010
to build this model for you.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:21.560
That is how simple machine
learning is with BigQuery ML.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:25.260
The technology was developed
by the Google Research team,

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.290
and we have brought it to
our BigQuery customers.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:31.050
To learn more, visit
the BigQuery website

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.330
and start doing machine
learning yourself

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.440
with just two lines of SQL.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.540
Thank you.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.290
[JINGLE PLAYING]

